#include \f[B]\(dqbashclient.h\(dq\f[R]

int bc_state_unset_var(bc_client_t *c, const char *name);
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Removes a shell variable from the bash\-server session associated with
the client connection \f[B]c\f[R].
After a successful call, the variable no longer exists in the
session\(cqs variable namespace.
.PP
The function sends an \f[CR]unset\f[R] request on the STATE channel
(\f[CR]CHAN_STATE\f[R], channel 2) with namespace \f[CR]\(dqvar\(dq\f[R]
and the given variable name.
The server performs the equivalent of \f[CR]unset name\f[R] in the shell
session.
.PP
If the variable does not exist, the server treats this as a successful
operation (no error is returned).
This matches the behavior of the \f[CR]unset\f[R] builtin in bash, which
succeeds silently when the target variable is not set.
.PP
If the variable has the \f[CR]readonly\f[R] attribute, the server
refuses the operation and returns an error.
