.SH NOTES
.IP \(bu 2
Unsetting a nonexistent variable is not an error.
This matches POSIX \f[CR]unset\f[R] semantics.
.IP \(bu 2
Unsetting a variable that has been exported also removes it from the
environment of subsequently executed child processes.
.IP \(bu 2
Special shell variables (e.g., \f[CR]BASH_VERSION\f[R],
\f[CR]RANDOM\f[R], \f[CR]LINENO\f[R]) may not be unsettable or may be
automatically re\-created by the shell.
The server\(cqs behavior in these cases matches the behavior of the
\f[CR]unset\f[R] builtin.
.IP \(bu 2
The function uses the v2 binary protocol.
The STATE channel request includes \f[CR]\(dqop\(dq: \(dqunset\(dq\f[R],
\f[CR]\(dqns\(dq: \(dqvar\(dq\f[R], and \f[CR]\(dqname\(dq\f[R] fields.
.IP \(bu 2
A single \f[CR]bc_client_t\f[R] must not be used concurrently from
multiple threads.
